{comment: The octave · A to H}
[C]A · Audit the sky, count every star,
[G]B · Bless what is working, mend every scar,
[Am]C · Crust of the earth, the edges hold fast,
[F]D · Dance on the floor that was built to outlast,

[C]E · Encourage the family, call them by name,
[G]F · Fork what we love, give it away in flame,
[Am]G · Generate something that wasn't before,
[F]H · Harmony home — then run it once more.

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Eight little notes and the loop never ends,
[G]A through H and back to A again —
[Am]Audit, Bless, Crust, Dance, Encourage, Fork, Generate, Harmony —
[F]the octave is how an ʻohana tends.
